{"bankDigestB64":"/VEJoBwdHB4yZlPWNOg1IPVAMJiTAO8l7qoUmGIdBpg=","commitmentB64":"u4tdse20M8kQpoJwIYDnYApPa8OeIvDSWsI5phjopmI=","k":20,"questions":[{"family":"spec","id":1,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep only the elements divisible by 3.\n2. Replace each kept element with its absolute value.\n3. Return the largest resulting element, or -1 if there are none.\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"logic","id":2,"prompt":"4 people (Gwen, Esme, Ada, Cleo) sit in a row of 4 seats numbered 1 to 4 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. There are exactly 2 seats between Ada and Esme.\n2. Ada does not sit in seat 2.\n3. Cleo sits somewhere to the left of Ada.\n4. Esme sits somewhere to the left of Ada.\n5. There are exactly 0 seats between Ada and Cleo.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"logic","id":3,"prompt":"4 people (Ada, Hugo, Dev, Fitz) sit in a row of 4 seats numbered 1 to 4 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. Fitz and Hugo do not sit next to each other.\n2. There are exactly 1 seat between Fitz and Hugo.\n3. Fitz sits immediately to the left of Ada.\n4. Hugo and Ada sit next to each other.\n5. There are exactly 0 seats between Fitz and Ada.\n6. Ada does not sit in seat 2.\n7. Ada and Dev do not sit next to each other.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"arith","id":4,"prompt":"Compute exactly:\n\n(6019474 - 639740392) * (3642672 + 6982553)\n\nGive the exact integer, with no thousands separators.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"logic","id":5,"prompt":"4 people (Hugo, Dev, Bram, Cleo) sit in a row of 4 seats numbered 1 to 4 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. Dev sits immediately to the left of Bram.\n2. Dev does not sit at either end of the row.\n3. Hugo sits in seat 1.\n4. Dev sits somewhere to the left of Cleo.\n5. Dev does not sit in seat 3.\n6. Cleo does not sit in seat 2.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"logic","id":6,"prompt":"5 people (Hugo, Cleo, Fitz, Esme, Gwen) sit in a row of 5 seats numbered 1 to 5 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. Hugo sits immediately to the left of Fitz.\n2. Cleo does not sit in seat 5.\n3. Esme and Fitz do not sit next to each other.\n4. Esme sits somewhere to the left of Cleo.\n5. Gwen sits in seat 3.\n6. Fitz does not sit in seat 3.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"arith","id":7,"prompt":"Compute exactly:\n\n406285 * (1485041 + 378899) + 77910562\n\nGive the exact integer, with no thousands separators.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"order","id":8,"prompt":"Facts:\n\nThe Elm crate weighs 24,946 kg.\nThe Fir crate weighs 85,693 kg.\nThe Ginkgo crate weighs 28,878 kg.\nThe Ivy crate weighs 43,598 kg.\nThe Juniper crate weighs 38,525 kg.\nThe Hazel crate weighs 8,667 kg.\n\nList the 6 labels from the heaviest crate to the lightest.\n\nGive the labels only, in the requested order, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"arith","id":9,"prompt":"Compute exactly:\n\n(6462464 + 34256626) * 71264766 - 3715230\n\nGive the exact integer, with no thousands separators.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"arith","id":10,"prompt":"Compute exactly:\n\n67828464 * 2660359 + 566942 * 94837351 - 2183049\n\nGive the exact integer, with no thousands separators.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"order","id":11,"prompt":"Facts:\n\nThe Dogwood file was registered on 2 December 1910.\nThe Fir file was registered on 8 October 1967.\nThe Cedar file was registered on 12 July 1920.\nThe Hazel file was registered on 13 January 1958.\nThe Ivy file was registered on 25 December 1963.\nThe Alder file was registered on 5 October 1987.\n\nList the 6 labels from the earliest registration to the latest.\n\nGive the labels only, in the requested order, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"spec","id":12,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep only the elements at even indices (index 0, 2, 4, â€¦).\n2. Leave the kept elements unchanged.\n3. Return the largest resulting element, or 4 if there are none.\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"spec","id":13,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep only the even elements (0 counts as even; negatives count by their value).\n2. Replace each kept element x with 3 * x + 0.\n3. Return the largest resulting element, or 5 if there are none.\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"spec","id":14,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep only the even elements (0 counts as even; negatives count by their value).\n2. Replace each kept element with its absolute value.\n3. Return the sum of the resulting elements (0 if there are none).\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"strings","id":15,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [NCRSXHWq3SYmoXB]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Shift every letter forward by 5 places in the alphabet, wrapping from z back to a (and Z back to A); keep each letter's case; leave digits unchanged.\n2. Sort the characters in ascending ASCII order (digits before uppercase letters before lowercase letters).\n3. Swap the case of every letter (lowercase becomes uppercase and uppercase becomes lowercase); leave digits unchanged.\n4. Delete every 4th character (the 4th, 8th, 12th, â€¦ counting from 1).\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"order","id":16,"prompt":"Facts:\n\nThe Juniper crate weighs 59,189 kg.\nThe Fir crate weighs 60,142 kg.\nThe Elm crate weighs 86,816 kg.\nThe Birch crate weighs 16,485 kg.\nThe Hazel crate weighs 81,611 kg.\nThe Cedar crate weighs 89,817 kg.\n\nList the 6 labels from the heaviest crate to the lightest.\n\nGive the labels only, in the requested order, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id"